      "text": "The total surface area of the pyramid includes the base and the 4 triangular faces. The area of the square base is side length squared: 10 cm * 10 cm = 100 cm^2.\n\nEach of the 4 triangular faces is a 45°-45°-90 triangle, since the triangle shares a right angle with the square. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the height of each face is √(10 cm * 10 cm) = 10 cm. The area of each triangular face is (base * height) / 2: (10 cm * 10 cm) / 2 = 50 cm^2.\n\nSince there are 4 triangular faces, the total surface area of the pyramid is 100 cm^2 + 50 cm^2/2 = 125 cm^2.\n\n$\\boxed{125}$",
